<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leopold Anton von Firmian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1679">1679</a>–<a href="/years/1744">1744</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leopold Anton von Firmian was prince-archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a> from 1727 to 1744. In 1731 he issued an edict expelling his Protestant subjects, and some 20,000 left, most of them settling in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-prussia">East Prussia</a> at the invitation of King Frederick William I. He also began the palace of Leopoldskron.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leopold-anton-von-firmian.jpg" alt="Leopold Anton von Firmian" width="320" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abp_Firmian_of_Salzburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
